silm:instances_papers_01_orientation_chapters_14_kleisli_enrichment_pipeline_sections_02_enrichment_by_type_information_yoneda_hom_leg_2 a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "EnrichmentLegLambdaClsExample" .
silm:instances_papers_01_orientation_chapters_14_kleisli_enrichment_pipeline_sections_02_enrichment_by_type_information_yoneda_hom_leg_2 silm:hasExample "In 'EnrichmentLegLambdaCls', the typed legs of the Yoneda hom-profile are witnessed by concrete Mittens-domain arrows. For example, JoC §6.18 (representability) plus JoC §3 (Set-enriched categories): the singleton hom-set Hom_O_01(Mittens, DomesticCat) = {lambda_cls} is a one-element object of Set. The Set-enrichment makes the typed hom-set explicit and small. For the Mittens fixture, lambda_cls is the categorical statement \"Mittens is a DomesticCat\"." .
